":"Rep. Levin, Mike [D-CA-49]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"D","sponsorshipDate":"2025-10-03","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"CA"},{"bioguideId":"W000831","fullName":"Rep. Walkinshaw, James R. [D-VA-11]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"D","sponsorshipDate":"2025-10-03","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"VA"},{"bioguideId":"L000557","fullName":"Rep. Larson, John B. [D-CT-1]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"D","sponsorshipDate":"2025-12-09","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"CT"},{"bioguideId":"E000296","fullName":"Rep. Evans, Dwight [D-PA-3]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"D","sponsorshipDate":"2025-12-16","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"PA"},{"bioguideId":"G000604","fullName":"Rep. Goodlander, Maggie [D-NH-2]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"D","sponsorshipDate":"2025-12-19","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"NH"},{"bioguideId":"T000486","fullName":"Rep. Torres, Ritchie [D-NY-15]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"D","sponsorshipDate":"2026-09-10","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"NY"}],"fetchedAt":"2026-09-16T20:55:58+00:00","id":"hr2799-119","introducedDate":"2025-04-09","latestAction":{"actionDate":"2025-04-09","text":"Referred to the Committee on the Judiciary, and in addition to the Committee on Ways and Means, for a period to be subsequently determined by the Speaker, in each case for consideration of such provisions as fall within the jurisdiction of the committee concerned."},"laws":[],"number":"2799","originChamber":"House","policyArea":"Crime and Law Enforcement","sponsors":[{"bioguideId":"T000468","district":1,"fullName":"Rep. Titus, Dina [D-NV-1]","party":"D","state":"NV"}],"summaries":[{"actionDate":"2025-04-09","actionDesc":"Introduced in House","text":"<p><strong>Closing the Bump Stock Loophole Act of 2025</strong></p><p>This bill&nbsp;generally prohibits the import, sale, manufacture, transfer, receipt, or possession of</p><ul><li>a device that is primarily designed, or redesigned, to increase the rate of fire when attached to a semiautomatic firearm;</li><li>a device, part, or combination of parts that is designed and functions to increase the rate of fire of a firearm; or</li><li>a semiautomatic firearm that has been modified to materially increase the rate of fire or to approximate the action or rate of fire of a machine gun.</li></ul><p>Additionally, the bill adds to the list of firearms subject to regulation under the National Firearms Act&nbsp;semiautomatic firearms&nbsp;that have been modified to materially increase the rate of fire or approximate the action or rate of fire of a machine gun.</p>","updateDate":"2026-03-24T15:28:13Z","versionCode":"00"}],"title":"Closing the Bump Stock Loophole Act of 2025","type":"hr","updateDate":"2026-09-11T08:05:33Z","updateDateIncludingText":"2026-09-11T08:05:33Z"}
